{
  "manufacturer": "SCC Inc.",
  "manufacturer_slug": "scc",
  "model": "TS-1100 touchscreen kit for Siemens LMV3 / LMV5 / RWF burner controls (BACnet IP / MS/TP)",
  "model_slug": "ts-1100-touchscreen-kit",
  "aliases": [
    "TS-1100",
    "TS1100",
    "TS Series touchscreen kit",
    "TS... touchscreen kit",
    "SCC TS-1100",
    "LMV5 BACnet",
    "LMV3 BACnet",
    "RWF55 BACnet",
    "RWF40 BACnet"
  ],
  "equipment_type": "Boiler burner management touchscreen with BMS gateway",
  "applies_to": "SCC TS-series touchscreen kits fitted with the optional QuickServer BMS gateway, serving Siemens LMV3/LMV5 burner controls, RWF40/RWF55/RWF10 controllers and the EA annunciator option.",
  "summary": "The TS-1100 touchscreen kit is an HMI for Siemens LMV3/LMV5 linkageless burner controls with an optional RWF load or water-level controller. Its optional gateway serves the same address list over BACnet IP and BACnet MS/TP: burner phase, actuator positions, flame, setpoints, lockout and error history, RWF and feedwater values, EA annunciator inputs, and writable remote mode, setpoint and firing-rate commands for the LMV and RWF.",
  "bacnet_transport": [
    "BACnet IP",
    "BACnet MS/TP"
  ],
  "firmware": null,
  "default_device_instance": 100,
  "access_inferred": false,
  "notes": [
    "The table lists AV/AO and BV/BO for the writable points; AO/BO are the Metasys N2 equivalents, so they are given here as AV and BV.",
    "AI 57 and AI 58 are both printed as FW_Current_SP (AI 57 is the feedwater E2 actual value).",
    "Some names are printed with a space after an underscore (e.g. \"LMV_EH_ Error_Code\", \"EA_ Ana_2_Total\"); kept as printed.",
    "The prose calls AV 21 LMV_Remote_Mode and AV 47 RWF_Remote_Mode; the table names are LMV_Rem_Mode and RWF_Command.",
    "Points marked LMV5... or LMV52... only carry data with those burner controls; RWF40 and EA points need those options.",
    "Units are not given in the table.",
    "This is the touchscreen's own optional BACnet gateway. The Contemporary Controls BASgatewayLX profile for the TS-1100 reads the same data over Modbus RTU but uses its own object numbering and names; see that list if a BASgatewayLX is fitted instead."
  ],
  "source": {
    "title": "TS Series Touchscreen Kits for use with LMV3, LMV5 and RWF... Controls - Installation Instructions",
    "doc_number": "TS-1100",
    "revision_date": "2014-07-18",
    "url": "https://ccontrols.com/support/dp/TS-1100_Installation_Instructions.pdf",
    "unofficial": true,
    "host": "Contemporary Controls (ccontrols.com)"
  },
  "integration": {
    "summary": "Keep BV 1 Active_Connection at 1 by rewriting it at least every 30 seconds, then pick a remote mode: AV 21 = 0 (auto) and write the setpoint to AV 22, or AV 21 = 1 (on) and write the firing rate to AV 23; AV 21 = 2 turns the LMV off. With an RWF, use AV 47 (1 setpoint, 2 full remote) with AV 48/AV 49. Read the burner phase, actual value, flame and alarm points for status.",
    "minimum_points": [
      {
        "ref": "AV 21",
        "name": "LMV_Rem_Mode",
        "why": "LMV remote mode: 0 auto, 1 on, 2 off"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 22",
        "name": "LMV_Remote_SP",
        "why": "Remote setpoint W3 (remote mode auto)"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 23",
        "name": "LMV_Rem_Output",
        "why": "Remote firing rate (remote mode on)"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BV 1",
        "name": "Active_Connection",
        "why": "BMS heartbeat; write 1 at least every 30 s"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BI 2",
        "name": "Available",
        "why": "Boiler available"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 1",
        "name": "LMV_Phase",
        "why": "LMV burner phase"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 12",
        "name": "LMV_Actual",
        "why": "Actual temperature / pressure (LMV5)"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 10",
        "name": "LMV_Current_Out",
        "why": "Current burner output"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BI 19",
        "name": "LMV_Alarm",
        "why": "LMV alarm"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 28",
        "name": "LMV_LO_Error_Code",
        "why": "Current lockout error code (LMV5)"
      }
    ],
    "enable": "Remote mode only works while BV 1 Active_Connection is held at 1 and the remote setpoint is above 0; the LMV local/remote mode then switches automatically. Writing BV 1 = 0 blocks remote mode.",
    "heartbeat": "BV 1 Active_Connection must be written to 1 at least once every 30 seconds; if it is not, the burner returns to local mode.",
    "remote_sensors": null,
    "setup": [
      "Default device instance 100 (set with DEV INS on the touchscreen Unit Type screen).",
      "BACnet IP uses UDP 47808; the gateway's default web address is 192.168.1.67 for changing its IP.",
      "BACnet MS/TP: default MAC 1, 38400 baud, set on the Unit Type screen.",
      "Protocol is chosen with the gateway DIP switches (BACnet IP or MS/TP profiles 1-4)."
    ],
    "gotchas": [
      "Full remote (firing rate) mode is not available on the RWF10; send the firing rate to the LMV3 instead.",
      "BV 35 RWF_Disable = 1 disables the RWF.",
      "AI and BI points are read-only; only the AV and BV points accept writes."
    ]
  },
